          "Ask about assessment, supported cleaning procedures, component repair or replacement and appropriate verification. The aim is to address the cause and restore correct operation where the vehicle and available service permit. Confirm the scope before authorizing work, including whether another specialist is needed.",
          "A warning light that has been suppressed does not demonstrate a successful repair. For road use, consider the vehicle’s emissions requirements and keep its emissions equipment functioning. The Environmental Management Bureau provides [Philippine Clean Air Act information](https://air.emb.gov.ph/the-philippine-clean-air-act/) covering the national emissions framework. A workshop assessment is not an emissions-test certificate or a guarantee of registration compliance."
