    "fullContent": "# Car Diagnostics, ECU Remapping and Repair Enquiries for Iloilo City\n\nIloilo City vehicle owners can contact Autohex ECU Tuning & Remapping to discuss warning lights, electronic faults, repair concerns and remapping compatibility. Send the make, model, year and symptoms before deciding which service to request. The first objective is to establish the right assessment and whether the vehicle is supported, especially when a fault has already led to unsuccessful parts replacements.\n\nThis page covers city-based enquiries and travel planning. It does not claim that Autohex has a workshop in every district or a city-centre branch. Request the current workshop pin and appointment directly before travelling toward the listed Oton location.\n\n## Different city starting points need different plans\n\nIloilo City’s [official planning documents](https://iloilocity.gov.ph/main/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/Vol1_CLUP-3-3-21-final-draft-1.pdf) identify districts including Mandurriao, Molo, Jaro and La Paz. The Iloilo River and its Esplanade also provide recognizable city context. These references help explain a starting area; they are not Autohex collection points or evidence of local branches.\n\nSay where the vehicle is currently located rather than only where you live. A car parked at work in Mandurriao may need a different travel arrangement from one at home elsewhere in the city. For district-specific planning around the business area, use the [Mandurriao page](/locations/iloilo-city/mandurriao/).\n\n## Choose diagnostics for a new problem\n\nA check-engine light, hesitation or intermittent stall should begin with an enquiry about [automotive diagnostics](/services/automotive-diagnostics/). Record when the fault appears, whether the engine is warm and what repairs preceded it. A fault code alone may not identify the component that needs replacement.\n\nIf a previous workshop suspects the engine computer, see [ECU repair assessment](/services/ecu-repair/). Ask what tests support the diagnosis and send the report. For wider controller concerns, describe the affected function rather than simply requesting “computer programming.” Different systems require different compatibility checks and procedures.\n\n## Discuss remapping as a separate goal\n\nIf the vehicle is running normally and you want to explore a calibration change, review [ECU remapping](/services/ecu-remapping/). Explain how you use the car, its modifications and what you hope to change. Ask about baseline checks and support for the exact engine and controller.\n\nCity traffic does not establish a guaranteed fuel-saving result. Consumption varies with usage, load, maintenance and driver inputs. Treat proposed gains as vehicle-specific and ask how they would be assessed. An existing warning or poor-running condition should be investigated before a performance change is considered.\n\n## Mechanical concerns and ongoing care\n\nFor a new noise, leak or physical fault, use [car repair](/services/car-repair/) and confirm the required work is available. Explain whether the vehicle can be moved safely. Serious braking issues, overheating or repeated stalling should not be treated as ordinary errands that can wait until a convenient drive past the workshop.\n\nKeep service records and mileage information available even when the main concern is electronic. Recent maintenance or a replacement part can be relevant to the symptom history. Ask what the initial inspection covers and how additional work will be quoted and authorized before it proceeds.\n\n## Plan travel from the city to Autohex\n\nIloilo City’s [planning information](https://iloilocity.gov.ph/main/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/CDP2023-2028_4-13_Final-Document.pdf) places Oton to its west, giving general orientation for a journey toward the listed workshop area. The best final approach depends on the current Autohex pin, your district and traffic. Use live navigation and request entrance instructions if this is your first visit.\n\nAvoid a fixed journey-time assumption, especially when coordinating a drop-off around work or another appointment. If the car may need to remain, arrange onward travel. Confirm transport separately if it cannot be driven safely. A service-area page does not promise emergency attendance, towing or collection from a mall, office or residence.\n\n## Send a useful first message\n\nContact the [Autohex Facebook page](https://www.facebook.com/AutohexEcuTuningRemapping) with the vehicle details, current district, warning photographs and previous test findings. State whether the problem is constant or intermittent. Include recent software changes, accessory installations and repair attempts where relevant.\n\nAsk about vehicle acceptance, assessment fees and appointment availability. If someone else will deliver the car, agree who will authorize repairs. Wait for a confirmed collection arrangement before returning, and request a clear account of findings and completed work for your records.\n\n## Questions from Iloilo City drivers\n\n### Is Autohex located inside Iloilo City?\nThe public listing reviewed places Autohex on C1 Road in Oton. Confirm the current workshop pin directly. This city page serves enquiries from city residents and does not establish a city branch.\n\n### Do you serve every district through mobile visits?\nMobile coverage is not established here. Ask about the available arrangement for your vehicle and location. An enquiry from Jaro, Molo or La Paz does not automatically include on-site attendance.\n\n### Should I use the Mandurriao page instead?\nUse it when your starting point or scheduling concern is specifically in Mandurriao. The service pages remain the main references for each type of work, and both location pages lead to the same business enquiry.",
